## What improved

- Prior blocker around Cursor `role:*` and `type:"human"` normalization is fixed.
- Cross-format tests were added for those specific cases.

## Remaining test gap

- No coverage yet for Gemini/Factory/OpenCode/Copilot transcript shapes in `compact` tests, so “any agent” behavior is still unproven.

PR: [entireio/cli#754](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/754)

## Findings

- **High — `Compact` still cannot handle native Gemini transcript message shape** (`cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact.go`)  
  `normalizeKind` now accepts `"gemini"` as assistant (good), but conversion still requires a nested `message` object. Native Gemini messages use top-level fields (`type`, `content`, etc.), so `parseMessage` returns `nil` and the converter emits mostly-empty lines (missing content, missing timestamps).  
  This contradicts the “any agent” goal.

```266:277:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact.go
func parseMessage(raw map[string]json.RawMessage) map[string]json.RawMessage {
	msgRaw, ok := raw["message"]
	if !ok {
		return nil
	}
	var msg map[string]json.RawMessage
	if json.Unmarshal(msgRaw, &msg) != nil {
		return nil
	}
	return msg
}
```

```182:199:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact.go
func convertAssistant(raw map[string]json.RawMessage, meta compactMeta) [][]byte {
	var id, content json.RawMessage
	if msg := parseMessage(raw); msg != nil {
		id = msg["id"]
		if contentRaw, ok := msg["content"]; ok {
			content = stripAssistantContent(contentRaw)
		}
	}
	// emits assistant line even when parseMessage == nil
```

```24:30:cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/transcript.go
type GeminiMessage struct {
	ID        string           `json:"id,omitempty"` // UUID for the message
	Type      string           `json:"type"`         // MessageTypeUser or MessageTypeGemini
	Content   string           `json:"content,omitempty"`
	ToolCalls []GeminiToolCall `json:"toolCalls,omitempty"`
}
```

- **Medium — Gemini tests currently validate only Claude-style wrapper, not native Gemini structure** (`cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact_test.go`)  
  The new Gemini tests use `{"type":"gemini","message":{...}}`, which won’t catch the real issue above.

```482:510:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact_test.go
// Gemini transcripts use type:"gemini" for assistant messages.
input := []byte(`{"type":"user","timestamp":"t1","message":{"content":"hello"}}
{"type":"gemini","timestamp":"t2","message":{"id":"g1","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Hi from Gemini!"}]}}
...
{"type":"gemini","timestamp":"t2","message":{"id":"g1","content":"It's 4."}}
`)
```

## Verification

- Ran `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/transcript` on local `convert-full-transcript` branch; tests pass.

If you want, I can draft the exact additional tests needed for native Gemini shape (top-level `content`/`toolCalls`) so this regression is caught.
